@najumon1980 @kristofer-jonsson-arm

Please briefly answer these questions:

* what problem are you trying to solve? (or if there's no problem, what's the motivation for this change?)

    `leader_retires` will invoke `CommandBoard::clear`, which will clear all command results in command board and then notify those wait task. 

    ```rust
    pub(super) fn release_notifiers(&mut self) {
        self.er_notifiers
            .drain()
            .for_each(|(_, event)| event.notify(usize::MAX));
        self.asr_notifiers
            .drain()
            .for_each(|(_, event)| event.notify(usize::MAX));
    }

    /// Clear
    pub(super) fn clear(&mut self) {
        self.er_buffer.clear();
        self.asr_buffer.clear();
        self.release_notifiers();
    }
    ```

    ```rust
    pub(super) async fn wait_for_er(
        cb: &CmdBoardRef<C>,
        id: &ProposeId,
    ) -> Result<C::ER, C::Error> {
        loop {
            if let Some(er) = cb.map_read(|cb_r| cb_r.er_buffer.get(id).cloned()) {
                return er;
            }
            let listener = cb.write().er_listener(id);
            listener.await;
        }
    }
    ```

    However, because it cannot obtain C::ER, it will once again enter a wait state and will not recover.
    Under certain extreme conditions, such as rapid GC of command board, this situation can also occur.

* what changes does this pull request make?

   `wait_for_xxx` will only wait once and return an `Option<...>`

* are there any non-obvious implications of these changes? (does it break compatibility with previous versions, etc)

